      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for trivy",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for trivy fixes the following issues:\n\nUpdate to version 0.76.2.\n\nSecurity issues fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-97045: golang.org/x/net/html: missing checks during ancestor namespace transitions when rendering raw\n  text can cause parser differentials (bsc#1289868).\n- CVE-2026-116585,CVE-2026-116586,CVE-2026-116587: github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4: multiple security issues in\n  github.com/go-jose/go-jose before 4.1.6 (bsc#1288377).\n\nOther updates and bugfixes:\n\n- Update `x/sys` to 0.50.0 to fix ppc64le syscall handling regression.\n- Version 0.76.2:\n * fix(deps): bump `golang.org/x/net` from 0.61.0 to 0.62.0 [backport: release/v0.76] (#11554)\n * chore(deps): bump the common group across 1 directory with 14 updates [backport: release/v0.76] (#11555)\n * fix(deps): bump `github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4` from 4.1.5 to 4.1.6 [backport: release/v0.76] (#11553)\n * fix(deps): bump `alpine` to 3.24.3 in container images [backport: release/v0.76] (#11551)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
