    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-97045",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-97045"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "In childTextNodesAreLiteral, walking up the tree previously stopped at the nearest foreign ancestor once an HTML integration point was found. However, that integration point may itself be a descendant of an element that was foster-parented into a foreign namespace (such as \u003cmglyph\u003e or \u003cmalignmark\u003e fostered under \u003cmtext\u003e), causing a parser to resolve the subtree in a different foreign namespace upon re-parsing the rendered output. Continue walking the full ancestor chain and verify that every transition from a non-empty namespace occurs at an HTML integration point before emitting literal text.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
      "product_status": {
        "recommended": [
          "openSUSE Leap 16.0:trivy-0:0.76.2-160000.1.1.aarch64",
